      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3438_Start4" name="Top-tier account; strategic milestone; relationship gap (W3429)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3438_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3438_Task5" name="Sponsor/Account Manager plan the executive engagement: identify customer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Sponsor/Account Manager plan the executive engagement: identify customer C-suite counterparts, map exec-to-exec relationships (W3429), set engagement objectives (relationship, strategic alignment, issue resolution), and design touchpoints (visits, events, briefings)
Responsible (R): Sponsor / Account Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Strategic Accounts
Duration: Per account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3438_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3438_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3438_Task6" name="Sponsor execute the engagement: site/store visits, executive briefings…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Sponsor execute the engagement: site/store visits, executive briefings, industry forums, BuildRight-hosted events (links to VS-14), and CSAT/NPS outreach (links to VS-13.1); capture insights and commitments
Responsible (R): Sponsor / Marketing
Accountable (A): CEO / COO
Duration: Per cadence</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3438_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3438_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3438_Task7" name="Account Manager document executive engagement in CRM (links to VS-13.3)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Account Manager document executive engagement in CRM (links to VS-13.3), cascade insights to the KAP (W3427) and QBR (W3430), and ensure continuity of exec relationships across sponsor changes; report engagement health to leadership
Responsible (R): Account Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Strategic Accounts
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3438_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
